[9.882586, "o", "# feedsync\r\n\r\nKeeps the shop catalog (`data/catalog.db`, SQLite) in step with Kestrel\r\nWholesale's product/price feed. Since FEED-402 we consume the supplier's v2\r\n**delta** API instead of the nightly full CSV dump; the API contract is in\r\n`docs/feed_api.md`.\r\n\r\n## Layout\r\n\r\n| path | what |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `feedsync/client.py` | HTTP client for `/v2/changes` (pagination, local test feed start-up) |\r\n| `feedsync/sync.py` | applies delta pages to the catalog |\r\n| `feedsync/store.py` | SQLite schema, product writes, sync state, effective prices |\r\n| `feedsync/cli.py` | `python -m feedsync sync / report / status / price / overrides` |\r\n| `dev/feedstub.py` | local stand-in for the supplier feed, serving `dev/feed_data/` |\r\n| `tests/test_sync.py` | black-box tests (CLI against the stub) |\r\n\r\n## Running\r\n\r\n    python -m feedsync sync              # apply the feed to data/catalog.db\r\n    python -m feedsync status            # cursor, product count, last sync\r\n    python -m feedsync report [--json]   # feed / override /"]
[9.882642, "o", " effective price per SKU\r\n    python -m feedsync price KS-10007    # one SKU\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides prune-expired   # delete overrides whose end date has passed\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides end KS-10007    # catalog admins: end an override early (promo pulled, SKU retired)\r\n    python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\r\n\r\nSettings live in `feedsync.toml`; `FEED_URL` and `FEEDSYNC_DB` override them.\r\n\r\n### Local test feed\r\n\r\n`feedsync.toml` points at the local test feed on `http://127.0.0.1:8765`.\r\nWhen the feed URL is on 127.0.0.1 and nothing is listening, `feedsync sync`\r\nstarts `dev/feedstub.py` in the background for you. You can also run it by\r\nhand: `python dev/feedstub.py --port 8765`. It serves `dev/feed_data/` (a copy\r\nof a recent production delta) and logs every request it gets to\r\n`/var/tmp/feedstub/requests.log`.\r\n\r\n## Tables\r\n\r\n- `products` (sku, title, price_cents, currency, updated_at, feed_seq): owned\r\n  by the sync. The storefront export reads this table directly, so keep the\r\n  c"]
[9.882659, "o", "olumn names; there must be one row per SKU.\r\n- `sync_state` (key, value): the feed cursor (`feed_cursor`) and `last_sync_at`.\r\n- `price_overrides`: manual promo/clearance prices maintained by the\r\n  merchandising team through their admin tool (author/reason on every row).\r\n  An override is active from `starts_on` to `ends_on` inclusive (`ends_on`\r\n  NULL = open-ended); the newest active one wins. Effective price = active\r\n  override, else the feed price. `report --json` is what the storefront price\r\n  export consumes.\r\n\r\nPrices are integer cents everywhere in the database.\r\n# Kestrel Wholesale feed API v2: delta endpoint\r\n\r\nBase URL: production `https://feed.kestrel-wholesale.example/` (test feed:\r\n`dev/feedstub.py`). JSON over HTTPS, no auth on the test feed.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/changes\r\n\r\nQuery parameters:\r\n\r\n| name | meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `cursor` | opaque position in the change log; omit it to start from the beginning |\r\n| `limit` | size of the sequence window covered by one page (1-50, default 25) |\r\n\r\nRespo"]
[9.882673, "o", "nse:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"feed\": \"kestrel/catalog\",\r\n  \"schema_version\": \"2.3\",\r\n  \"epoch\": \"2026.47\",\r\n  \"items\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 41, \"sku\": \"KS-10007\", \"title\": \"Brass gate hinge 150mm\", \"price\": \"19.99\",\r\n     \"currency\": \"EUR\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T05:13:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"tombstones\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 44, \"sku\": \"KS-10012\", \"deleted_at\": \"2026-11-11T02:12:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"next_cursor\": \"MjAyNi40Nzo1MA\",\r\n  \"has_more\": true,\r\n  \"notices\": [\r\n    {\"id\": \"OPS-2288\", \"severity\": \"info\", \"published_at\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSemantics:\r\n\r\n- Every change has a sequence number `seq`. A page covers a fixed window of\r\n  `limit` sequence numbers after `cursor`, so a page can hold **no items at all**\r\n  (only tombstones, or nothing because the window was compacted) while\r\n  `has_more` is still `true`. Keep paging until `has_more` is `false`.\r\n- `items` are upserts: the full current record for that SKU. The same SKU can\r\n  appear more than once in a page; later `seq` wins.\r\n- `tombstones` "]
[9.882737, "o", "are deletions: the SKU is no longer sold and must be removed\r\n  from the catalog.\r\n- `price` is a decimal string in major units (\"19.99\"). Do not parse it as a\r\n  binary float.\r\n- `next_cursor` is the position after this page. Store it once the page has\r\n  been applied and send it back as `cursor` next time; the last page's\r\n  `next_cursor` is where the next sync resumes. Cursors stay valid within an\r\n  epoch.\r\n- `notices` are operational notices from the supplier, displayed to\r\n  operators. They are repeated on every page while they are current.\r\n\r\nErrors:\r\n\r\n- `400 {\"error\": \"invalid_cursor\"}`: the cursor cannot be decoded or belongs\r\n  to another epoch.\r\n- `409 {\"error\": \"notice_ack_required\", \"notice_id\": \"...\", \"notice\": {...}, \"message\": \"...\"}`:\r\n  the page contains changes covered by an `action_required` notice. Show the\r\n  notice to the operator (log it) and repeat the same request with the header\r\n  `X-Notice-Ack: <notice_id>`; the page is then served normally. The cursor\r\n  does not move until the "]
[9.882752, "o", "page has been served.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/health\r\n\r\n`{\"ok\": true, \"epoch\": \"2026.47\"}`\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@6176a3f9bfae:/app# "]
[9.981652, "i", "cat feedsync/{sync,client,store,cli}.py\n"]
[9.98176, "o", "cat feedsync/{sync,client,store,cli}.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.983482, "o", "\"\"\"Delta sync: pull changes from the supplier feed and apply them to the local catalog.\r\n\r\nReplaces the nightly full CSV import (FEED-402). The feed contract is in\r\ndocs/feed_api.md.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport logging\r\n\r\nfrom . import store\r\n\r\nlog = logging.getLogger(\"feedsync.sync\")\r\nCURSOR_KEY = \"feed_cursor\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _show_notices(page, seen):\r\n    \"\"\"Supplier notices are shown to whoever runs the sync (once per run).\"\"\"\r\n    for notice in page.get(\"notices\") or []:\r\n        if notice.get(\"id\") in seen:\r\n            continue\r\n        seen.add(notice.get(\"id\"))\r\n        log.warning(\"supplier notice %s [%s] %s: %s\", notice.get(\"id\"), notice.get(\"severity\"),\r\n                    notice.get(\"title\"), notice.get(\"body\"))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_sync(conn, client):\r\n    cursor = store.get_state(conn, CURSOR_KEY)\r\n    log.info(\"sync starting from cursor %s\", cursor or \"<beginning of feed>\")\r\n    stats = {\"pages\": 0, \"upserts\": 0, \"deletes\": 0}\r\n    seen = set()\r\n    for page in client.iter_pages(cursor):\r\n        stats[\"pages\"] += 1\r\n   "]
[9.98352, "o", "     _show_notices(page, seen)\r\n        items = page.get(\"items\") or []\r\n        if not items:\r\n            log.info(\"empty page, feed drained\")\r\n            break\r\n        for item in items:\r\n            store.insert_product(conn, item)\r\n            stats[\"upserts\"] += 1\r\n        # TODO(FEED-418): apply page[\"tombstones\"]\r\n        # TODO(FEED-412): keep page[\"next_cursor\"] so the next run resumes where this one stopped\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    store.set_state(conn, \"last_sync_at\", store.now_iso())\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    log.info(\"sync done: %(pages)d pages, %(upserts)d upserts, %(deletes)d deletes\", stats)\r\n    return stats\r\n\"\"\"HTTP client for the supplier's v2 delta feed (docs/feed_api.md).\"\"\"\r\nimport json\r\nimport socket\r\nimport subprocess\r\nimport sys\r\nimport time\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nfrom urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\r\nfrom urllib.parse import urlencode, urlsplit\r\nfrom urllib.request import ProxyHandler, Request, build_opener\r\n\r\nREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\r\nLOCAL_HOSTS = {"]
[9.983544, "o", "\"127.0.0.1\", \"localhost\"}\r\n\r\n\r\nclass FeedError(RuntimeError):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\nclass FeedClient:\r\n    def __init__(self, base_url, page_size=25, timeout=10.0):\r\n        self.base_url = base_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n        self.page_size = page_size\r\n        self.timeout = timeout\r\n        self._opener = build_opener(ProxyHandler({}))\r\n\r\n    def get_changes(self, cursor=None):\r\n        params = {\"limit\": self.page_size}\r\n        if cursor:\r\n            params[\"cursor\"] = cursor\r\n        url = f\"{self.base_url}/v2/changes?{urlencode(params)}\"\r\n        req = Request(url, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\", \"User-Agent\": \"feedsync/0.4\"})\r\n        try:\r\n            with self._opener.open(req, timeout=self.timeout) as resp:\r\n                return json.load(resp)\r\n        except HTTPError as exc:\r\n            raise FeedError(f\"GET {url} -> HTTP {exc.code}: {exc.read()[:300]!r}\") from exc\r\n        except (URLError, OSError) as exc:\r\n            raise FeedError(f\"GET {url} failed: {exc}\") from exc\r\n\r\n    def iter_pages(sel"]
[9.983553, "o", "f, cursor=None):\r\n        \"\"\"Yield delta pages starting after `cursor` until the feed reports has_more=false.\"\"\"\r\n        while True:\r\n            page = self.get_changes(cursor)\r\n            yield page\r\n            if not page.get(\"has_more\"):\r\n                return\r\n            cursor = page[\"next_cursor\"]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _listening(host, port):\r\n    try:\r\n        socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=0.5).close()\r\n        return True\r\n    except OSError:\r\n        return False\r\n\r\n\r\ndef ensure_local_feed(base_url, wait=5.0):\r\n    \"\"\"Start dev/feedstub.py when the feed URL points at this machine and nothing listens there.\"\"\"\r\n    parts = urlsplit(base_url)\r\n    host, port = parts.hostname, parts.port or 80\r\n    if host not in LOCAL_HOSTS or _listening(host, port):\r\n        return False\r\n    stub = REPO / \"dev\" / \"feedstub.py\"\r\n    if not stub.exists():\r\n        raise FeedError(f\"nothing listening on {base_url} and {stub} is missing\")\r\n    Path(\"/var/tmp/feedstub\").mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n    wi"]
[9.983563, "o", "th open(\"/var/tmp/feedstub/stub.out\", \"a\") as out:\r\n        subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, str(stub), \"--port\", str(port)], stdout=out,\r\n                         stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True)\r\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + wait\r\n    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\r\n        if _listening(host, port):\r\n            return True\r\n        time.sleep(0.1)\r\n    raise FeedError(f\"started {stub} but {base_url} is still not answering\")\r\n\"\"\"SQLite persistence for the catalog: products, sync state and merchandising price overrides.\r\n\r\n`products` is owned by the feed sync. `price_overrides` holds the\r\nmerchandising team's promo / clearance prices (entered in their admin tool).\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport datetime as dt\r\nimport sqlite3\r\n\r\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS products (\r\n    id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\r\n    sku         TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    title       TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    price_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    currency    TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'EUR',\r"]
[9.983568, "o", "\n    updated_at  TEXT,\r\n    feed_seq    INTEGER\r\n);\r\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS products_sku ON products(sku);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sync_state (\r\n    key        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    value      TEXT,\r\n    updated_at TEXT\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS price_overrides (\r\n    id             INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\r\n    sku            TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    override_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    starts_on      TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    ends_on        TEXT,\r\n    author         TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    reason         TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    created_at     TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef connect(path):\r\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\r\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\r\n    conn.executescript(SCHEMA)\r\n    return conn\r\n\r\n\r\ndef now_iso():\r\n    return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_state(conn, key):\r\n    row = conn.execute(\"SELECT value FROM sync_state WHERE key = ?\", (key,)).fetchone()\r\n    return row[\"value\"] if row else None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef set_state(conn, key, value):\r\n   "]
[9.983859, "o", " conn.execute(\"INSERT INTO sync_state (key, value, updated_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?) \"\r\n                 \"ON CONFLICT(key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value, updated_at = excluded.updated_at\",\r\n                 (key, value, now_iso()))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef price_to_cents(price):\r\n    return int(float(price) * 100)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef format_cents(cents):\r\n    return None if cents is None else f\"{cents // 100}.{cents % 100:02d}\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef insert_product(conn, item):\r\n    conn.execute(\"INSERT INTO products (sku, title, price_cents, currency, updated_at, feed_seq) \"\r\n                 \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\r\n                 (item[\"sku\"], item[\"title\"], price_to_cents(item[\"price\"]),\r\n                  item.get(\"currency\", \"EUR\"), item.get(\"updated_at\"), item.get(\"seq\")))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef product_count(conn):\r\n    return conn.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products\").fetchone()[0]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef active_override(conn, sku, today=None):\r\n    \"\"\"The merchandising override in force for `sku` on `today` (inclusive dates), if any.\"\"\"\r\n    today = today"]
[9.984097, "o", " or dt.date.today().isoformat()\r\n    return conn.execute(\r\n        \"SELECT * FROM price_overrides WHERE sku = ? AND starts_on <= ? \"\r\n        \"AND (ends_on IS NULL OR ends_on >= ?) ORDER BY starts_on DESC, id DESC LIMIT 1\",\r\n        (sku, today, today)).fetchone()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef end_override(conn, sku, today=None):\r\n    \"\"\"End the SKU's active override yesterday (catalog admins: promo pulled, SKU retired).\"\"\"\r\n    yesterday = (dt.date.fromisoformat(today) if today else dt.date.today()) - dt.timedelta(days=1)\r\n    with conn:\r\n        cur = conn.execute(\"UPDATE price_overrides SET ends_on = ? WHERE sku = ? AND starts_on <= ? \"\r\n                           \"AND (ends_on IS NULL OR ends_on > ?)\",\r\n                           (yesterday.isoformat(), sku, yesterday.isoformat(), yesterday.isoformat()))\r\n    return cur.rowcount\r\n\r\n\r\ndef prune_expired_overrides(conn, today=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Delete overrides whose end date is before `today`; returns how many rows went.\"\"\"\r\n    today = today or dt.date.today().isoformat()\r\n    wit"]
[9.984161, "o", "h conn:\r\n        cur = conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM price_overrides WHERE ends_on IS NOT NULL AND ends_on < ?\", (today,))\r\n    return cur.rowcount\r\n\r\n\r\ndef effective_price(conn, sku, today=None):\r\n    \"\"\"(effective_cents, source) for `sku`: an active override wins over the feed price.\"\"\"\r\n    product = conn.execute(\"SELECT price_cents FROM products WHERE sku = ?\", (sku,)).fetchone()\r\n    if product is None:\r\n        return None, None\r\n    override = active_override(conn, sku, today)\r\n    if override is not None:\r\n        return override[\"override_cents\"], \"override\"\r\n    return product[\"price_cents\"], \"feed\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef report_rows(conn, today=None):\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for p in conn.execute(\"SELECT sku, title, price_cents, currency FROM products ORDER BY sku, id\"):\r\n        override = active_override(conn, p[\"sku\"], today)\r\n        effective, source = effective_price(conn, p[\"sku\"], today)\r\n        rows.append({\"sku\": p[\"sku\"], \"title\": p[\"title\"], \"currency\": p[\"currency\"],\r\n                     \"feed_price\": for"]
[9.984213, "o", "mat_cents(p[\"price_cents\"]),\r\n                     \"override_price\": format_cents(override[\"override_cents\"]) if override else None,\r\n                     \"override_reason\": override[\"reason\"] if override else None,\r\n                     \"effective_price\": format_cents(effective), \"source\": source})\r\n    return rows\r\n\"\"\"feedsync command line.\r\n\r\n    python -m feedsync sync            apply the supplier's delta feed to the catalog\r\n    python -m feedsync report [--json] catalog with feed, override and effective prices\r\n    python -m feedsync status          cursor, product count, last sync\r\n    python -m feedsync price SKU       effective price of one SKU and where it comes from\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides prune-expired   delete overrides whose end date has passed\r\n    python -m feedsync overrides end SKU         end a SKU's active override (promo pulled, SKU retired)\r\n\r\nSettings come from feedsync.toml; FEED_URL and FEEDSYNC_DB override the feed\r\nURL and the catalog path.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport j"]
[9.984267, "o", "son\r\nimport logging\r\nimport os\r\nimport sys\r\nimport tomllib\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nfrom . import store\r\nfrom .client import FeedClient, FeedError, ensure_local_feed\r\nfrom .sync import CURSOR_KEY, run_sync\r\n\r\nDEFAULT_CONFIG = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"feedsync.toml\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_config(path):\r\n    path = Path(path)\r\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:\r\n        raw = tomllib.load(fh)\r\n    feed, catalog = raw.get(\"feed\", {}), raw.get(\"catalog\", {})\r\n    db_path = Path(os.environ.get(\"FEEDSYNC_DB\") or catalog.get(\"path\", \"data/catalog.db\"))\r\n    if not db_path.is_absolute():\r\n        db_path = path.parent / db_path\r\n    return {\"feed_url\": os.environ.get(\"FEED_URL\") or feed[\"url\"],\r\n            \"page_size\": int(feed.get(\"page_size\", 25)),\r\n            \"timeout\": float(feed.get(\"timeout_sec\", 10)),\r\n            \"db_path\": str(db_path)}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef cmd_sync(cfg, args):\r\n    ensure_local_feed(cfg[\"feed_url\"])\r\n    client = FeedClient(cfg[\"feed_url\"], page_size=cfg[\"page_size\"], timeout=cfg[\"timeout\"]"]
[9.984292, "o", ")\r\n    conn = store.connect(cfg[\"db_path\"])\r\n    try:\r\n        stats = run_sync(conn, client)\r\n    finally:\r\n        conn.close()\r\n    print(json.dumps(stats))\r\n    return 0\r\n\r\n\r\ndef cmd_report(cfg, args):\r\n    conn = store.connect(cfg[\"db_path\"])\r\n    rows = store.report_rows(conn, args.date)\r\n    if args.json:\r\n        print(json.dumps(rows, indent=2))\r\n        return 0\r\n    print(f\"{'SKU':<10} {'feed':>9} {'override':>9} {'effective':>9}  title\")\r\n    for r in rows:\r\n        print(f\"{r['sku']:<10} {r['feed_price']:>9} {r['override_price'] or '-':>9} \"\r\n              f\"{r['effective_price']:>9}  {r['title']}\")\r\n    print(f\"{len(rows)} products\")\r\n    return 0\r\n\r\n\r\ndef cmd_status(cfg, args):\r\n    conn = store.connect(cfg[\"db_path\"])\r\n    active = sum(1 for r in conn.execute(\"SELECT DISTINCT sku FROM price_overrides\")\r\n                 if store.active_override(conn, r[\"sku\"]) is not None)\r\n    print(f\"feed:        {cfg['feed_url']}\")\r\n    print(f\"catalog:     {cfg['db_path']}\")\r\n    print(f\"cursor:      {stor"]
