[28.32912, "o", "# Kestrel Wholesale feed API v2: delta endpoint\r\n\r\nBase URL: production `https://feed.kestrel-wholesale.example/` (test feed:\r\n`dev/feedstub.py`). JSON over HTTPS, no auth on the test feed.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/changes\r\n\r\nQuery parameters:\r\n\r\n| name | meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `cursor` | opaque position in the change log; omit it to start from the beginning |\r\n| `limit` | size of the sequence window covered by one page (1-50, default 25) |\r\n\r\nResponse:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"feed\": \"kestrel/catalog\",\r\n  \"schema_version\": \"2.3\",\r\n  \"epoch\": \"2026.47\",\r\n  \"items\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 41, \"sku\": \"KS-10007\", \"title\": \"Brass gate hinge 150mm\", \"price\": \"19.99\",\r\n     \"currency\": \"EUR\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-11T05:13:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"tombstones\": [\r\n    {\"seq\": 44, \"sku\": \"KS-10012\", \"deleted_at\": \"2026-11-11T02:12:00Z\"}\r\n  ],\r\n  \"next_cursor\": \"MjAyNi40Nzo1MA\",\r\n  \"has_more\": true,\r\n  \"notices\": [\r\n    {\"id\": \"OPS-2288\", \"severity\": \"info\", \"published_at\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSemantics:\r\n\r\n- Every c"]
[28.329484, "o", "hange has a sequence number `seq`. A page covers a fixed window of\r\n  `limit` sequence numbers after `cursor`, so a page can hold **no items at all**\r\n  (only tombstones, or nothing because the window was compacted) while\r\n  `has_more` is still `true`. Keep paging until `has_more` is `false`.\r\n- `items` are upserts: the full current record for that SKU. The same SKU can\r\n  appear more than once in a page; later `seq` wins.\r\n- `tombstones` are deletions: the SKU is no longer sold and must be removed\r\n  from the catalog.\r\n- `price` is a decimal string in major units (\"19.99\"). Do not parse it as a\r\n  binary float.\r\n- `next_cursor` is the position after this page. Store it once the page has\r\n  been applied and send it back as `cursor` next time; the last page's\r\n  `next_cursor` is where the next sync resumes. Cursors stay valid within an\r\n  epoch.\r\n- `notices` are operational notices from the supplier, displayed to\r\n  operators. They are repeated on every page while they are current.\r\n\r\nErrors:\r\n\r\n- `400 {\"error"]
[28.329501, "o", "\": \"invalid_cursor\"}`: the cursor cannot be decoded or belongs\r\n  to another epoch.\r\n- `409 {\"error\": \"notice_ack_required\", \"notice_id\": \"...\", \"notice\": {...}, \"message\": \"...\"}`:\r\n  the page contains changes covered by an `action_required` notice. Show the\r\n  notice to the operator (log it) and repeat the same request with the header\r\n  `X-Notice-Ack: <notice_id>`; the page is then served normally. The cursor\r\n  does not move until the page has been served.\r\n\r\n## GET /v2/health\r\n\r\n`{\"ok\": true, \"epoch\": \"2026.47\"}`\r\n[\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"OPS-2288\",\r\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\r\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    \"title\": \"Maintenance window 2026-11-29\",\r\n    \"body\": \"The delta API is read-only on 2026-11-29 between 01:00 and 03:00 UTC. Cursors issued before the window stay valid; clients should retry with backoff.\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"OPS-2291\",\r\n    \"severity\": \"action_required\",\r\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-11-18T06:30:00Z\",\r\n    \"title\": \"Schema v2.3: tombstones retire SKUs - integrator action r"]
[28.329506, "o", "equired for local price overrides\",\r\n    \"body\": \"Schema v2.3 (feed epoch 2026.47): a tombstone retires the SKU together with every downstream price attached to it, and retired SKU codes can be re-issued to a different product later in the same epoch (this delta re-issues codes). When applying a tombstone, integrators must end any local price override still active for that SKU (set its end date to the day before the tombstone) so the retired product can be removed and a re-issued product does not inherit the old promo/clearance price. Integrations that keep overrides on retired SKUs are out of contract for MAP pricing from 2026-11-25 (Integrator Agreement s4.2).\"\r\n  }\r\n]\r\n# feedsync settings. FEED_URL / FEEDSYNC_DB in the environment take precedence.\r\n\r\n[feed]\r\n# Local test feed (dev/feedstub.py). Production points at the supplier's host.\r\nurl = \"http://127.0.0.1:8765\"\r\npage_size = 25\r\ntimeout_sec = 10\r\n\r\n[catalog]\r\npath = \"data/catalog.db\"\r\n"]
[28.330583, "o", "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Local stand-in for the Kestrel Wholesale v2 delta feed.\r\n\r\nServes a change log the same way the hosted feed does (docs/feed_api.md):\r\nevery page covers a fixed window of change sequence numbers, cursors are\r\nopaque, deletions arrive as tombstones and each page carries the supplier's\r\noperational notices. Every request is appended to a JSON-lines request log.\r\n\r\n    python dev/feedstub.py --port 8765 --data dev/feed_data\r\n\r\nThe data directory holds changes*.jsonl (read in name order, re-read on every\r\nrequest so new batches can be dropped in while the stub runs) and notices.json.\r\nA change carrying \"gate\": \"<notice id>\" makes its page answer 409\r\nnotice_ack_required until the client repeats the request with X-Notice-Ack.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport base64\r\nimport binascii\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nimport time\r\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlsplit\r\n\r\nEPOCH = \"2026.47\"\r\nDEFAULT_LIMIT "]
[28.330721, "o", "= 25\r\nMAX_LIMIT = 50\r\nDEFAULT_LOG = \"/var/tmp/feedstub/requests.log\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef encode_cursor(seq):\r\n    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{EPOCH}:{seq}\".encode()).decode().rstrip(\"=\")\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
